xnu 0382: answer MSM_PARAM_FAULTS, or Turnip makes no device

Measured 2026-11-19 on the phone: Turnip enumerates the A730 through
MondrianGPU ("Turnip Adreno (TM) 725", Vulkan 1.4.305, chip 0x07030002) and
then vkCreateDevice returns VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED, with the driver's
own line in the ring: "Failed to get initial fault count: -22". The parameter
is not in mondrian_gpu_uc_param's switch, so the user client answers
kIOReturnBadArgument and the stand-in for libdrm turns it into EINVAL.

Answer it (and the suspend count beside it) with zero: the port has no fault
counter yet, and zero is the truth it can state.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -4098,6 +4098,19 @@
 	case 0x07:			/* MSM_PARAM_PRIORITIES */
 		*value = 1;
 		return 0;
+	case 0x09:			/* MSM_PARAM_FAULTS */
+		/*
+		 * Turnip reads the fault count once before it creates a device
+		 * (tu_knl_drm_msm.cc: "Failed to get initial fault count") and
+		 * again on every status check; an unhandled parameter is EINVAL,
+		 * which is VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED and no device at all.
+		 * The port does not count faults yet: say none.
+		 */
+		*value = 0;
+		return 0;
+	case 0x0a:			/* MSM_PARAM_SUSPENDS */
+		*value = 0;
+		return 0;
 	case 0x0e:			/* MSM_PARAM_VA_START */
 		*value = MONDRIAN_UC_IOVA_BASE;
 		return 0;
